{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_015vPYnejjJgsDdwZKyW78Tv", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag_day_(computing)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Network_Control_Protocol_(ARPANET)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.tribuneindia.com/news/anniversary/birth-of-the-internet-a-historic-development-in-communications\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.tribuneindia.com/news/anniversary/birth-of-the-internet-a-historic-development-in-communications/amp\"}, {\"url\": \"https://elists.isoc.org/pipermail/internet-history/2009-November/000960.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://elists.isoc.org/pipermail/internet-history/2009-November/000961.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://elists.isoc.org/pipermail/internet-history/2009-November/000967.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://elists.isoc.org/pipermail/internet-history/2023-August/008772.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://jisaku.com/glossary/tcp-ip-transition-1983\"}, {\"url\": \"https://internetnews.com/news/30-years-of-tcp-ip-dominance-began-with-a-deadline\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:16:54.515Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "ARPANET flag day January 1 1983 NCP to TCP/IP", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_016RM7DrQX1CsFnURM47BcwA", "content": [{"title": "Flag day (computing)", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag_day_(computing)"}, {"title": "Network Control Protocol (ARPANET)", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Network_Control_Protocol_(ARPANET)"}, {"title": "birth of the internet a historic development in communications", "url": "https://www.tribuneindia.com/news/anniversary/birth-of-the-internet-a-historic-development-in-communications"}, {"title": "Add Tribune As Your Trusted Source", "url": "https://www.tribuneindia.com/news/anniversary/birth-of-the-internet-a-historic-development-in-communications/amp"}, {"title": "[ih] internet-history Digest, Vol 37, Issue 1", "url": "https://elists.isoc.org/pipermail/internet-history/2009-November/000960.html"}, {"title": "[ih] internet-history Digest, Vol 37, Issue 1", "url": "https://elists.isoc.org/pipermail/internet-history/2009-November/000961.html"}, {"title": "[ih] internet-history Digest, Vol 37, Issue 1", "url": "https://elists.isoc.org/pipermail/internet-history/2009-November/000967.html"}, {"title": "[ih] Memories of Flag Day?", "url": "https://elists.isoc.org/pipermail/internet-history/2023-August/008772.html"}, {"title": "TCP/IP Flag Day Transitionとは?(ティーシーピーアイピーフラッグデー)意味・特徴をわかりやすく解説 | 自作.com | PC自作用語集 - 自作.com", "url": "https://jisaku.com/glossary/tcp-ip-transition-1983"}, {"title": "30 Years of TCP/IP Dominance Began with a Deadline", "url": "https://internetnews.com/news/30-years-of-tcp-ip-dominance-began-with-a-deadline"}]}, "The search results confirm the January 1, 1983 cutover, with a few details worth noting.\n\n- **The transition itself:** Wikipedia's article on the NCP protocol says the ARPANET changed its core networking protocols from NCP to TCP/IP on January 1, 1983, in what is known as a flag day. The flag day article describes it as a transition that took place on a fixed date.\n- **Preparation:** Per the same NCP article, backbone routers disabled NCP traffic for most hosts on several days toward the end of 1982 to test the network's readiness. A former IMP implementer's posting on the Internet-history list describes adding a per-port setting that let IMPs discard NCP packets for ports not approved for NCP use (index 8-10 to 8-12).\n- **Holdouts:** The NCP article notes that a number of sites continued use of NCP into mid-1983.\n- **Scale:** A 2009 InternetNews retrospective puts the host count at roughly 400, and argues that today's scale makes a similar flag day impractical (index 10-6 to 10-8).\n- **Framing:** Bob Braden, in a 2009 Internet-history message, recalled that people reckoned the beginning of the Internet to be the Red Flag day when the ARPAnet converted from NCP to TCP/IP (index 5-8).\n\nOne caveat: a Tribune India piece calls TCP/IP's development a Cerf and Kahn effort, which is consistent with the standard history, but it is a general news article rather than a primary source."], "durationSeconds": 7.124806042000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_015vPYnejjJgsDdwZKyW78Tv", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgDZ2AE2cRTLFhbNVhonh", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**答案：1983 年 1 月 1 日。** 这一天是 ARPANET 的 “Flag Day”，网络的核心协议从 NCP 全部换成了 TCP/IP。1982 年底，骨干路由器曾在几天里对大多数主机关掉 NCP，测试网络是否准备好了。切换日之后，还有一些站点把 NCP 用到了 1983 年年中。\n\n我只搜了 1 次。\n\n来源：\n- [Network Control Protocol (ARPANET) – Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Network_Control_Protocol_(ARPANET))\n- [Flag day (computing) – Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag_day_(computing))\n- [30 Years of TCP/IP Dominance Began with a Deadline – InternetNews](https://internetnews.com/news/30-years-of-tcp-ip-dominance-began-with-a-deadline)"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1392, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4298, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1392}, "output_tokens": 331, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:16:58.740Z", "request_id": "req_011CgDZ29uvapXx81XvfS3Mo"}
